  "question": {
    "text": "A planet revolves about the sun in elliptical orbit of semi-major axis <math> <mrow> <mn>2</mn><mo>×</mo><msup> <mrow> <mn>10</mn></mrow> <mrow> <mn>12</mn></mrow> </msup> <mtext>m</mtext><mo>.</mo></mrow> </math> The areal velocity of the planet when it is nearest to the sun is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo>.4</mo><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>16</mn></msup><mo>&nbsp;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>/</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math>.The least distance between planet and the sun is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>.8</mo><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>12</mn></msup><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>. The minimum speed of the planet in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>km</mi><mo>/</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math>. Value of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math>&nbsp;is",
    "image": null
  },
